 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "West Wind, bring to us a delicate wind\nFrom the boundless deeps of the ages behind,\nAnd breathe it upon the arid beaches\nWhere we are with our daughters.\nStoop down at our feet again,\nThe dark-haired one that was not young before.\nShe is old; her long hair rises,\nBreathing sweetly and quietly.\nGush downward from out the foamless waters\nOn to her full breasts the soft breezes\nThat whisper sighing songs again,\nTill she is like one insane.",
